{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula","id":1282771,"title":"The actual origin of Dracula?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-01-25T19:45:10-08:00","id":1282771,"title":"The actual origin of Dracula?","content":"From what I can recall from &quot;Rites of the Dragon&quot;, I think it used the Francis Cord Coppla backstory for Dracula saying he was cursed by God and such but what if I decided to discard all that and instead went with the actual Bram Stoker's Dracula as exactly described in the novel especially where he really got his Vampirism from which was from Black Magic and Alchemy that he learned from the Scholomance and he's not even Kindred at all but a entirely different type of Vampire altogether hence explains why he can walk in the sun unharmed but weakened by it, but is automatically repelled and harmed by Catholic imagery no matter how much faith the wielder has, has no reflection, can't show up in cameras, has no shadow and even portraits of his likeness crumble over time, has red blazing inferno eyes when he engages in vampiric acts or becomes angered, he becomes aged and apparently weak if he goes long periods of time without drinking blood but becomes younger (and perhaps stronger) if he does but his hands are hairy and clawed, cannot enter a home without invitation, cannot cross running water, must sleep in his native soil, but is extremely powerful however? Plus he has no beast nor humanity system either.<br /> <br /> Hence the Kindred made a convenient based around him trying to become just like their supposed &quot;Founder&quot; that is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","user":"Black Blood","date":". 01-25-2019, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","name":"Black Blood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T10:33:02-08:00","id":1282873,"title":"","content":"You can play with his origin as much as you like. In fact modern Kindred can and probably should be concerned whether Dracula existed at all as the Coils he supposedly invented were spread by his &quot;brides&quot;. Dracula himself is enough of an enigma you can write him in as you please. <br /> <br /> Almost everything you list could be explained by banes, taken to stave off the degradation of Humanity. High Humanity would enable him to walk in the sunlight even. You could back that up with a supernatural merit or two--or a Coil, and then he won't be melting in the sun at all. <br /> <br /> I'd keep the Beast and Humanity system. Just because Dracula doesn't frenzy in the book doesn't mean he's not struggling with what is the core game mechanic issue.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T10:38:47-08:00","id":1282877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula?p=1282873#post1282873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd keep the Beast and Humanity system. Just because Dracula doesn't frenzy in the book doesn't mean he's not struggling with what is the core game mechanic issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it does mean he's not struggling with the Beast because he doesn't have one since he's not Kindred at all but a completely different type of Vampire that is entirely unique.<br /> <br /> Since having Dracula as a typical Kindred not only cheapens his significance but also makes the game more boringly predictable.<br /> <br /> Just because the Beast/Humanity system is the core game mechanic doesn't mean it wholly defines what a Vampire is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","user":"Black Blood","date":". 01-26-2019, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","name":"Black Blood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T13:40:30-08:00","id":1282903,"title":"","content":"Pretty much anything is possible in Chronicle of Darkness and this wouldn't be the first vampire that's unlike the splat as we know it (see <i>Night Horrors: The Wicked Dead</i>). If Dracula was that fundamentally different from other vampires (despite <i>a lot</i> of superficial similarities), then what exactly is his significance to V:tR, let alone the Ordo Dracul?<br /> <br /> Besides, your description could also fit a strix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 01-26-2019, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T13:52:19-08:00","id":1282905,"title":"","content":"Dracula having no shadow? That's odd, according to my memory, the story of Dracula usually depicts him having a shadow that appears to have taken on a life of its own, being able to function independently of him.<br /> <br /> That might just be a movie thing, though?<br /> <br /> <br /> If we're talking about his ability to move in sunlight, that was actually the case for the original European vampire as well. The death by sunlight weakness didn't come into the picture until the Nosferatu movie, at which point, the story of vampires were retconned to include not being able to withstand the sun.<br /> <br /> I think Dracula was killed by stabbing him in the heart with a silver knife, as opposed to a wooden stake?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-26-2019, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T14:07:51-08:00","id":1282909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula?p=1282905#post1282905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dracula having no shadow? That's odd, according to my memory, the story of Dracula usually depicts him having a shadow that appears to have taken on a life of its own, being able to function independently of him.<br /> <br /> That might just be a movie thing, though?<br /> <br /> <br /> If we're talking about his ability to move in sunlight, that was actually the case for the original European vampire as well. The death by sunlight weakness didn't come into the picture until the Nosferatu movie, at which point, the story of vampires were retconned to include not being able to withstand the sun.<br /> <br /> I think Dracula was killed by stabbing him in the heart with a silver knife, as opposed to a wooden stake?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dracula having no shadow is from the book which is one of the few details that hardly anyone pays attention to outside of pop culture.<br /> <br /> Also he was originally killed by first having his throat slashed by Harker and Quincy stabbed him with a Bowe Knife through the heart and he crumbled to dust since it took several men to kill him since he wouldn't go down without a fight. The Stake in the Heart was from the 1931 Bela Lugosi film.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula?p=1282903#post1282903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much anything is possible in Chronicle of Darkness and this wouldn't be the first vampire that's unlike the splat as we know it (see <i>Night Horrors: The Wicked Dead</i>). If Dracula was that fundamentally different from other vampires (despite <i>a lot</i> of superficial similarities), then what exactly is his significance to V:tR, let alone the Ordo Dracul?<br /> <br /> Besides, your description could also fit a strix.</div> </div> </div> </div>Highly doubt Dracula is a Strix but a rather unique type of Vampire via occultist means.<br /> <br /> I always thought that other Kindred idolized and envied how unique Dracula was who doesn't have a beast, can walk in the sun, and how powerful he was which they formed a research group dedicated to studying him (and other non-Kindred vampires) which later became the Ordo Dracul which could be possible that the Founders of the Ordo-Dracul found the Scholomance which is how they developed the coils.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","user":"Black Blood","date":". 01-26-2019, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","name":"Black Blood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T16:14:19-08:00","id":1282920,"title":"","content":"This seems a bad idea. You're basically removing the philosophical depth to the Ordo Dracul, replacing it with copying some random monster who isn't even a kindred. Plus, his limitations are really bad. His one advantage is the sunlight thing, but pretty much everything else is a step down. What's there to idolise?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T20:39:40-08:00","id":1282953,"title":"","content":"I guess this means having Dracula as exactly described in the novel in Reqiuem is almost impossible to implement unless one invents a really, really good explanation.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's possible that the Founder of the Ordo Dracul was of Dr\u0103cule\u0219ti bloodline but maybe not Vlad the Impaler himself but rather <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mircea_III_Dracul\" target=\"_blank\">Mircea III Dracul</a> was the one who was embraced and founded the Covenant whilst Vlad Tepes II Dracul was the one who obtained vampirism via the Scholomance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","name":"Black Blood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T02:17:09-08:00","id":1282991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Blood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula?p=1282953#post1282953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess this means having Dracula as exactly described in the novel in Reqiuem is almost impossible to implement unless one invents a really, really good explanation.</div> </div> </div> </div>It very much depends what your objective is. I mean, in most games, Dracula is only present in setting mythology. A kindred can read Dracula and wonder if the being presented is actually one of the kindred, and whether that matches their organisations founder, but that's more or less it. What's the aim of this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T07:51:36-08:00","id":1283043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula?p=1282991#post1282991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It very much depends what your objective is. I mean, in most games, Dracula is only present in setting mythology. A kindred can read Dracula and wonder if the being presented is actually one of the kindred, and whether that matches their organisations founder, but that's more or less it. What's the aim of this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure a Kindred can read Dracula and wonder if the being presented is one of their own but things are not what they seem to be though that's the point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","name":"Black Blood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T14:00:17-08:00","id":1283115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Blood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula?p=1283043#post1283043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure a Kindred can read Dracula and wonder if the being presented is one of their own but things are not what they seem to be though that's the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but you still haven't said why that would matter to an actual game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T14:36:22-08:00","id":1283126,"title":"","content":"Wasn't it suggested in one of Dark Eras that Dracula was actually cursed by God-Machine?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1191-rosencroft","name":"Rosencroft","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T20:12:36-08:00","id":1283177,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blck Blood</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">he really got his Vampirism from which was from Black Magic and Alchemy that he learned from the Scholomance</div> </div> </div> </div>The origins of our vampire myth are of a bloothirsty-shapeshifting witch, and I really like this as an origin for Dracula. That said...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Blood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula?p=1282909#post1282909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Highly doubt Dracula is a Strix but a rather unique type of Vampire via occultist means.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I actually kind of like the idea of Dracula as being a Strix. Those witch origins for vampires *are* the Strix -- and I think that fits more with the Strix than the kindred. In <i>Gangrel:Savage and Macabre, </i>the Strix are described as sorcerers and a kind of sibling to the precursors to the Gangrel. And in the corebook, we're told that there are in fact several different species of Strix -- and the corebook tells us that the only surefire way of telling the difference between a kindred and a Strix is that Strix will survive sunlight. Further, vampires as reanimated corpses comes out of Transylvania/Romania and (doing a quick search of Strix/Rose posts) she mentions that the Kindred in Transylvania went to war with the Strix and that is where a lot of our vampire mythology comes from. Coded information about Strix.<br /> <br /> So it might make sense that the most iconic, Transylvanian vampire is a Strix. But rather than the chaos causing, aimless vampires, Dracula is more in the vein of The Baron or Varney the Vampire. He is very old, and has been in one body long enough to do strange things to it... So what the hell is he doing with the Ordo? I know there is a fanmade Coil that is based on making the kindred more strix-like...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Blood</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always thought that other Kindred idolized and envied how unique Dracula was who doesn't have a beast, can walk in the sun, and how powerful he was which they formed a research group dedicated to studying him (and other non-Kindred vampires) which later became the Ordo Dracul which could be possible that the Founders of the Ordo-Dracul found the Scholomance which is how they developed the coils.</div> </div> </div> </div>But yeah, if you're not feeling the strix-origin, what direction were you thinking of taking it? How were you thinking of having it play out in a game? That Dracula did something to himself at Scholomance, and the Ordo alter themselves in similar ways to create the Coils? Does that mean that the Coils could actually work on humans? In this case, who are <i>The Brides? </i>Could they be a trio of vampires who captured and now experiment on this semi-uber-vampire? Could they be his cultists?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24634,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","user":"DubiousRuffian","date":".  formatting and elaboration on Gangrel/Strix 01-28-2019, 02:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T22:33:28-08:00","id":1283203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DubiousRuffian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula?p=1283177#post1283177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The origins of our vampire myth are of a bloothirsty-shapeshifting witch, and I really like this as an origin for Dracula. That said...<br /> <br /> I actually kind of like the idea of Dracula as being a strix. Those witch origins for vampires *are* the strix -- and I think that fits more with the strix than the kindred. In <i>Gangrel:Savage and Macabre, </i>the strix are described as a kind of sibling to the precursors to the Gangrel. And in the corebook, we're told that there are in fact several different species of strix -- and the corebook tells us that the only surefire way of telling the difference between a kindred and a strix is that strix will survive sunlight. Further, vampires as reanimated corpses comes out of Transylvania/Romania and (doing a quick search of Strix/Rose posts) she mentions that the Kindred in Transylvania went to war with the Strix and that is where a lot of our vampire mythology comes from. Coded information about Strix.<br /> <br /> So it might make sense that the most iconic, Transylvanian vampire is a Strix. But rather than the chaos causing, aimless vampires, Dracula is more in the vein of The Baron or Varney the Vampire. He is very old, and has been in one body long enough to do strange things to it... So what the hell is he doing with the Ordo? I know there is a fanmade Coil that is based on making the kindred more strix-like...</div> </div> </div> </div>Then again I have a feeling that shoehorning Dracula to either Kindred or Strix shoehorns extra baggage that isn't present in the original novel which means I'm better off presenting him as exactly how he is from the novel 100% including his origins as exactly described in the novel hence making him entirely unique and not exactly Strix nor Kindred at all but a entirely different or rather more powerful and unique strain of Vampirism that only he himself obtained making him stand out amongst other Vampires.<br /> <br /> Although Sarah Kenyon from &quot;The Tomb of Sarah&quot; might fit closest to a Strix though more than Dracula however which is perhaps the most scariest Vampire story I've ever read myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","name":"Black Blood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T00:16:11-08:00","id":1283214,"title":"","content":"In general, the &quot;truth&quot; of Dracula in Chronicles is actually something of a deliberate mystery-even the Rites of the Dragon are subject to being subjective interpretation or even a lie that Dracula doesn't realize is such(this was back when the Fog of Ages was a thing) or any number or other things. Even the light mention of possible intervention by the God-Machine is not a settled affair, and even if it is, there's a distance between such an event and the formation of the Ordo or the defeat of Dracula that any number of name-bearers could step into.<br /> <br /> This is important for the mentality of the Ordo Dracul and the rest of vampire society by extension-Dracula as a physical entity is nowhere near as important as Dracula as a mutating, changing ideal. There could have been a thousand Draculas, all telling a thousand lies about who they were, and it is the mutability and terrible possibility in all of that that is important. Dracula represents the myriad stories of the vampires, the Strix and the Kindred and more asides, and the frightening possibility all and none of them are true. He is a nightmare in the dark, an impossibility made real by the incarnation of the Clans, the Bloodlines, and deeper still the Mysteries. He's a whisper from a friend of a friend of a friend, and maybe even half of it is true, and wouldn't that be terrifying.<br /> <br /> So the more accurate way to approach the basic idea of the thread is &quot;Which Dracula do you want to be true?&quot;<br /> <br /> Cause yeah, there was a Dracula. There were <i>lots</i> of Draculas. There will be <i>more</i> Draculas. At the end of the day, they'll all end up as being the many and one Dracula.<br /> <br /> As for Stoker's, probably some kind of Kindred with a shit ton of Banes and a lot of history. Or not-the mistake over how common an epithet Dracula was in the area and time was just as prevalent then as it is now.(And that's speaking historically)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T05:45:03-08:00","id":1283237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula?p=1283214#post1283214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Stoker's, probably some kind of Kindred with a shit ton of Banes and a lot of history. Or not-the mistake over how common an epithet Dracula was in the area and time was just as prevalent then as it is now.(And that's speaking historically)</div> </div> </div> </div>Stoker's Dracula can't be a Kindred because he doesn't have a beast nor does he suffer sunlight damage at all which is why I'm suggesting he's a entirely different type of vampire altogether well just like Carmilla for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","name":"Black Blood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T06:58:14-08:00","id":1283249,"title":"","content":"Or maybe he developed Coils that straight up removed those weaknesses. I mean, that's a huge part of what Ordo Dracul is all about, and if anyone has mastered the Mysteries to the point where weaknesses are removed instead of just reworked into more manageable levels it would most certainly be Dracula.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T06:58:56-08:00","id":1283250,"title":"","content":"Just to nitpick - Carmilla is a Daeva in-setting. She's some kind of invictus royalty, and seems to be considered something of a brat princess.<br /> <br /> Also for Dracula as a unique vampire species, I dig it. I think there's a lot of potential for playing around with the idea that there are all these different &quot;Dracula stories&quot; - little 'd' draculas whose stories might have gotten mixed into the original story - maybe the Order establishment thinks the story changed with the telling, or tried to explain away differences between Book Dracula and standard Kindred, but it turns out that there is just The Dracula, and he is everything we hoped he would be. Kind of like a vampire version of Unforgiven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T07:00:03-08:00","id":1283251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula?p=1283249#post1283249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or maybe he developed Coils that straight up removed those weaknesses. I mean, that's a huge part of what Ordo Dracul is all about, and if anyone has mastered the Mysteries to the point where weaknesses are removed instead of just reworked into more manageable levels it would most certainly be Dracula.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe Dracula is a title, kind of like 'Buddha'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T08:28:52-08:00","id":1283270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DubiousRuffian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula?p=1283250#post1283250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to nitpick - Carmilla is a Daeva in-setting. She's some kind of invictus royalty, and seems to be considered something of a brat princess..</div> </div> </div> </div>Then again though, I don't think Carmilla is a Kindred either especially if you're going by the original book because she doesn't suffer sunlight damage nor does she have a beast at all but just with uncontrolled romantic passions and blood thirst that she has yet to control not to mention she has a rosy healthy complexion and is warm that can pass off as mortal whose alive not deathly pale as Kindred or majority of Vampires are and has a faint beating heart and has to sleep in a coffin or confined space full of her victims blood as well. Not to mention she also has a reflection, shadow, can show up in camera etc unlike Dracula and of course from what I'm aware of, the Kindred in Requiem don't have a reflection or don't show up on cameras but only their clothes show I guess.<br /> <br /> Matter of fact sunlight damage didn't come until F.W. Murnau's Nosferatu but yet all the Kindred and all of their so called &quot;diverse&quot; bloodlines suffer sunlight damage and the beast/frenzy making them not so diverse as they first appear especially in the face of much grander vampire literature and folklore that is which is more evident that the Kindred all have a single origin due to these universal traits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","user":"Black Blood","date":". 01-28-2019, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","name":"Black Blood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T08:47:36-08:00","id":1283278,"title":"","content":"Kindred can replicate a living person's complexion via Blush of Life and cast a reflection if they choose. <br /> Stoker's Dracula was prone to abrupt fits of rage over petty shit as well as having his schemes thwarted.<br /> If you insist that Stoker's Dracula is really a lich, I would suggest looking up the Tremere legacy in Mage if you want to use World of Darkness mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T08:53:16-08:00","id":1283280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula?p=1283278#post1283278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stoker's Dracula was prone to abrupt fits of rage over petty shit as well as having his schemes thwarted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then again that had nothing to do the beast/frenzying there but more like he's just a ruthless jerk in the book (since you know the actual Vlad Tepes II was a warlord voivode in life you know) and of course his glow inferno red everytime he does this along with engaging in vampiric acts (well rather like how Otto Goezti from Paul Feval's &quot;Vampire City&quot; glows green when engaging in vampiric activities especially) or displaying power that is but still under control unlike a Kindred in Frenzy who are more bestial/feral.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula?p=1283278#post1283278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you insist that Stoker's Dracula is really a lich, I would suggest looking up the Tremere legacy in Mage if you want to use World of Darkness mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then again, a Lich isn't a Vampire but aren't they Walking Skeleton Necromancers though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","user":"Black Blood","date":". 01-28-2019, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","name":"Black Blood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T09:16:00-08:00","id":1283283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Blood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula?p=1283280#post1283280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026but still under control unlike a Kindred in Frenzy who are more bestial/feral.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frenzy isn't the same as werewolves' Kuruth. Several of the books (in particular the clanbooks and Wicked Dead, though they're 1e, but also some of the 2e flavor) describe the Beast as being capable of careful hunting as well as just raw destruction: after all, the Beast is what gives a Mekhet Auspex and Obfuscate. Why would it just throw away all that subtlety in order to slap at someone with Strength 1 Brawl 0?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Blood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula?p=1283280#post1283280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then again, a Lich isn't a Vampire but aren't they Walking Skeleton Necromancers though?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're walking skeletons in D&amp;D; in CofD, the term means a mage who's achieved a sort of immortality at the cost of consuming human souls. So they normally just look like, well, mages. (Except creepier because they eat lots of souls.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T09:39:48-08:00","id":1283289,"title":"","content":"Only Reaper liches eat souls. Other types of liches do body hopping when their current body is about to give out, or transform themselves to an ephemeral entity (which comes with certain side effects). There's no single type of lich and they can look pretty different. The most basic life-extending kind will just look like they always did or continue ageing beyond the point when they should've died of natural causes, depending on how exactly they do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T10:10:10-08:00","id":1283299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula?p=1283283#post1283283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frenzy isn't the same as werewolves' Kuruth. Several of the books (in particular the clanbooks and Wicked Dead, though they're 1e, but also some of the 2e flavor) describe the Beast as being capable of careful hunting as well as just raw destruction: after all, the Beast is what gives a Mekhet Auspex and Obfuscate. Why would it just throw away all that subtlety in order to slap at someone with Strength 1 Brawl 0?</div> </div> </div> </div>However during the state of frenzy, the Kindred is basically possessed by their beasts and they have no control what they're doing, while Dracula in the novel does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula?p=1283278#post1283278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kindred can replicate a living person's complexion via Blush of Life and cast a reflection if they choose.</div> </div> </div> </div>However it requires blood points being spent much like using disciplines and not a permanent built-in feature like Carmilla has. Much like walking in sunlight unharmed is a built in feature for Carmilla, Dracula, Ruthven, etc which they don't have to use disciplines or anything like Kindred do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","user":"Black Blood","date":". 01-28-2019, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","name":"Black Blood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T12:39:05-08:00","id":1283330,"title":"","content":"Just because you never see Dracula frenzy doesn't mean he has no Beast.<br /> <br /> Just because Carmilla is always seen with Blush of Life active doesn't mean it's a constant built-in feature for her. Or it could be something from a Bloodline, even.<br /> <br /> Of course, any Kindred who has a book written about them has strong motives to change as many strengths/weaknesses displayed in the text as they can. And with Kindred (and books) as old as those two, they have plenty of time to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T12:59:48-08:00","id":1283334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula?p=1283330#post1283330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because you never see Dracula frenzy doesn't mean he has no Beast.<br /> <br /> Just because Carmilla is always seen with Blush of Life active doesn't mean it's a constant built-in feature for her. Or it could be something from a Bloodline, even.<br /> <br /> Of course, any Kindred who has a book written about them has strong motives to change as many strengths/weaknesses displayed in the text as they can. And with Kindred (and books) as old as those two, they have plenty of time to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or maybe it's time to stop assuming every Vampire is a Kindred by default since I rather treat Kindred as a particular strain/variation of vampirism which Dracula and Carmilla don't belong to hence why they never frenzy and Carmilla always has blush of life built into her because it's specific to their own variation of vampirism.<br /> <br /> Hence Dracula's and Carmilla's vampirism are more &quot;superior&quot; and polished via a occultist stance than your typical Kindred mainly because they have no beast and their powers are more fluid and more powerful than simple disciplines (although they also have many weaknesses which is a price to pay for great power) and plus they can walk in the sun unlike Kindred do.<br /> <br /> Also Ruthven and Varney clearly are not Kindred at all because they can be killed through normal means but they can always resurrect through the rays of a full moon hence they have no permanent &quot;Final Death&quot; as long the Full Moon is present which is another feature that Kindred don't have either because once a Kindred dies, they die permanently unlike Dracula, Ruthven, Varney and possibly even Carmilla which they can be resurrected via different means (Full Moon for Ruthven and Varney and Blood sacrifices for Dracula and Carmilla or any Vampire of Karnstein bloodline).<br /> <br /> Also get this too, Ruthven and Clarimonde have no fangs either and apparently all Kindred have fangs unless they're ripped out of them but I guess I assume they regrow them though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","user":"Black Blood","date":". 01-28-2019, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","name":"Black Blood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T13:01:14-08:00","id":1283335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Blood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula?p=1283334#post1283334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or maybe it's time to stop assuming every Vampire is a Kindred by default since I rather treat Kindred as a particular strain/variation of vampirism which Dracula and Carmilla don't belong to.</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd be easier if you actually explained what you're trying to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T13:15:01-08:00","id":1283338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula?p=1283335#post1283335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It'd be easier if you actually explained what you're trying to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm basically brainstorming a hypothetical setting where Vampirism exists as various snowflakes from each other in the CoD setting with Kindred as they are presented vanilla are one of them among many others.<br /> <br /> Not actually running a game or anything but just putting certain thoughts out there you know.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","user":"Black Blood","date":". 01-28-2019, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","name":"Black Blood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T13:42:46-08:00","id":1283349,"title":"","content":"Well, there are various types of vampires in the Requiem setting beyond kindred. I believe one of the night horrors books (and the upcoming one) had chapters dedicated to them; my personal favorite was the little parasitic creature that would replace someone's tongue and pretty much go onto control their minds and bodies for the sole purpose of infecting more people with parasites. On a side note, Kindred show up fuzzy in cameras and mirrors if they aren't actively paying enough attention for an accurate picture to be taken.<br /> <br /> Now, in my games the title of Dracula has always been just that: a title. Various kindred have had it, and various vampires have had it. Now if you wanted to keep the classics (Dracula, Carmilla, etc.) as purely kindred, obscure bloodlines and occultic methods to increase their power (which the Coils of the Ordo definitely count as) then that works out. There's actually one written up bloodline with access to resurrection, and one scale of the wyrm has a way to provide it as well.<br /> <br /> Now, if you wanted to make them other types of vampires beyond kindred, that's also fine. I know of one type of vampire called the Blood Bathers that showed up in the Immortals book from 1e (they also show up in dark eras as well). They basically each had rituals for extending their lives and some of the rituals even granted power, but they were ultimately still living creatures. I could see Carmilla being a blood bather. I also recall one group of vampires called Ghuls (I probably didn't spell that right) that were also still living creatures that had access to powerful magicks in exchange for having to eat human flesh (Dracula might fit under this theoretically, but I think we could find something better). We've also got the strix, your classic dead guy rises from the grave possessed by an evil spirit vampire.<br /> <br /> So yeah, Requiem presents the idea that there are various types of vampires. I believe Kindred still have their place as some of the toughest and most mutable vampires out there though, since their form of immortality is honestly the most reliable form that we generally see in the Requiem, or even some other splats (outside of the Purified shamans, of course). So I wouldn't at all consider them weak vampires, all things considered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T14:31:21-08:00","id":1283361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula?p=1283349#post1283349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, in my games the title of Dracula has always been just that: a title. Various kindred have had it, and various vampires have had it. Now if you wanted to keep the classics (Dracula, Carmilla, etc.) as purely kindred, obscure bloodlines and occultic methods to increase their power (which the Coils of the Ordo definitely count as) then that works out. There's actually one written up bloodline with access to resurrection, and one scale of the wyrm has a way to provide it as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it should be obvious by now that I don't want Dracula, Carmilla, etc being Kindred nor Strix at all which is the main point of this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","name":"Black Blood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T14:37:48-08:00","id":1283365,"title":"","content":"I'm a fan of the idea that Dracula is a Beast (the Primordial kind) with Kinship with vampires (the Brides).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T14:42:51-08:00","id":1283367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula?p=1283365#post1283365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a fan of the idea that Dracula is a Beast (the Primordial kind) with Kinship with vampires (the Brides).</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, him being a Beast would contradict some important details.<br /> <br /> I rather him being a entirely different unique &quot;breed&quot; of Vampire that is not Kindred nor Strix but someone who has obtained immortality via occultist means and of course his &quot;Brides&quot; (Rather called &quot;Strange Sisters&quot; in the book) and Lucy are his Thralls who are nothing more than extensions of his will pretty much hence that's no description of a Kindred right there since Kindred embrace and the Vampires they turn are individuals even if they're blood bounded but Vampires that &quot;turned&quot; by Dracula automatically become his thralls under his control where Dracula is the &quot;Master Vampire&quot; and &quot;One stronger still&quot; that is.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","user":"Black Blood","date":". 01-28-2019, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","name":"Black Blood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T14:47:40-08:00","id":1283368,"title":"","content":"I know its not a perfect fit, I just like the idea anyway. Thought I'd toss it out there for the thread since I hadn't seen it here yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T15:23:34-08:00","id":1283373,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7348\" data-vbnamecard=\"7348\">Black Blood</a><br /> <br /> if you read Rites of the Dragon and the Ordo Dracul Covenant book more carefully, you'll actually see some subtle but every clear evidence that Dracula is just an ordinary Kindred, embraced like any other Kindred, with a sire just like any other Kindred.<br /> <br /> Okay, ordinary is not the right word, Dracula is far from ordinary, but that's because of his feats as an extraordinary person. He's special because his accomplishments and feats are special, not because he's inherently unique.<br /> <br /> Dracula, in Vampire the Requiem, was mostly likely embraced by a brutish (Turkish?) warrior, the one who attacked him with the Ottomans on the night of his betrayal. Based on his abilities in Rites of the Dragon, I'd say Dracula is a Gangrel, but that's just an educated guess, given how often he relies on Protean to get the job done.<br /> <br /> Dracula also has a Beats just like any other Kindred, and struggles against frenzy, like any other Kindred. Rites of the Dragon is not even ambiguous about that. He constantly describes how he struggles against his inner Beast, especially when he's dealing with those three hunters who invaded his castle (did anyone else think of Castlevania during that chapter or was it just me?).<br /> <br /> Dracula also comes to stand face to face with his own Beast during a dream at the end of Rites of the Dragon, where his Beast takes the shape of an actual dragon during his dreams.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> I get that Dracula being an ordinary Gangrel would raise some questions that need answering, such as why his sire never showed up, and why his brides don't seem to have any blood sympathy with any of the clans. That's fair enough. To answer that question in my own Requiem game set in Victorian London, I decided to convert Clan Tzimisce from Vampire the Masquerade to Vampire the Requiem. I decided that Dracula did not raise as a full Kindred the night of his death. No, he rose as a Revenant instead. As a revenant, he sought out a way to become a clanned vampire. How he did this, I do not want to spoil in case any of my players read this, but suffice to say, Dracula is the first vampire of Clan Tzimisce in my Requiem game.<br /> <br /> Here is my own homebrew and my customized lore for Clan Tzimisce for my Requiem game: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17HAFXr4_ScMQksA5IZpGnFIuu5mukVhL18JAYm7JZwo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 01-28-2019, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T15:37:29-08:00","id":1283374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula?p=1283373#post1283373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7348\" data-vbnamecard=\"7348\">Black Blood</a><br /> <br /> if you read Rites of the Dragon and the Ordo Dracul Covenant book more carefully, you'll actually see some subtle but every clear evidence that Dracula is just an ordinary Kindred, embraced like any other Kindred, with a sire just like any other Kindred.<br /> <br /> Okay, ordinary is not the right word, Dracula is far from ordinary, but that's because of his feats as an extraordinary person. He's special because his accomplishments and feats are special, not because he's inherently unique.<br /> <br /> Dracula, in Vampire the Requiem, was mostly likely embraced by a brutish (Turkish?) warrior, the one who attacked him with the Ottomans on the night of his betrayal. Based on his abilities in Rites of the Dragon, I'd say Dracula is a Gangrel, but that's just an educated guess, given how often he relies on Protean to get the job done.<br /> <br /> Dracula also has a Beats just like any other Kindred, and struggles against frenzy, like any other Kindred. Rites of the Dragon is not even ambiguous about that. He constantly describes how he struggles against his inner Beast, especially when he's dealing with those three hunters who invaded his castle (did anyone else think of Castlevania during that chapter or was it just me?).<br /> <br /> Dracula also comes to stand face to face with his own Beast during a dream at the end of Rites of the Dragon, where his Beast takes the shape of an actual dragon during his dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes I know about that which I actually reject everything that has been written in &quot;Rites of the Dragon&quot; entirely which I prefer using Dracula exactly how he's described in the novel 100% right down to his origins that he got his particular form of vampirism at the scholomance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","user":"Black Blood","date":". 01-28-2019, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","name":"Black Blood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T15:53:09-08:00","id":1283378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Blood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula?p=1283374#post1283374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes I know about that which I actually reject everything that has been written in &amp;quot;Rites of the Dragon&amp;quot; entirely which I prefer using Novel Dracula as exactly he's described in the book 100% right down to his origins that he got his particular form of vampirism at the scholomance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Students who attended the Scholomance were already strigoi before they attended. So if Dracula was a blood drinking witch then there\u2019s nothing requiring him to be an undead vampire any more than a bokor is required to be a zombie simply because he spawns them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T16:05:15-08:00","id":1283380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula?p=1283378#post1283378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Students who attended the Scholomance were already strigoi before they attended. So if Dracula was a blood drinking witch then there\u2019s nothing requiring him to be an undead vampire any more than a bokor is required to be a zombie simply because he spawns them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you got it all wrong since I don't think I remember reading any of that but rather what I'm aware is that the &quot;Devil&quot; selects 10 students to become Solomonars which I assume are mortals and his lets the other nine go and keeps the tenth one to ride Dragons and control weather pretty much.<br /> <br /> Since Vlad attended the scholomance when he was mortal (I remember seeing a comic on kickstarter where he attended the scholomance as a child or teenager actually) just his peers did and studied and performed black magic and alchemy and lived his mortal life until he got killed and then he rose to life as a Vampire afterwords due to the rituals/magic he performed in life which is assuming how it went.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","user":"Black Blood","date":". 01-28-2019, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","name":"Black Blood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T16:19:03-08:00","id":1283381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Blood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula?p=1283374#post1283374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes I know about that which I actually reject everything that has been written in &quot;Rites of the Dragon&quot; entirely which I prefer using Dracula exactly how he's described in the novel 100% right down to his origins that he got his particular form of vampirism at the scholomance.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17HAFXr4_ScMQksA5IZpGnFIuu5mukVhL18JAYm7JZwo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Then I urge you again to give my homebrew Requiem Clan Tzimisce a look</a>. While I tried to stay within the canon given by Rites of the Dragon, I also tried to incorporate a lot of Bram Stoker's Dracula into my personal take on Clan Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> There is no mention of Scholomance in my write-up, but then again, I kept the origin of the Clan purposefully vague, so the Clan might very well be the result of hellish sorcery. It would work well with the idea that Dracula rose as a Revenant originally, and got initiated into Clan Tzimisce at Scholomance.<br /> <br /> If you don't like my work, that's fine. I'm just trying to help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T16:26:22-08:00","id":1283383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula?p=1283381#post1283381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17HAFXr4_ScMQksA5IZpGnFIuu5mukVhL18JAYm7JZwo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Then I urge you again to give my homebrew Requiem Clan Tzimisce a look</a>. While I tried to stay within the canon given by Rites of the Dragon, I also tried to incorporate a lot of Bram Stoker's Dracula into my personal take on Clan Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> There is no mention of Scholomance in my write-up, but then again, I kept the origin of the Clan purposefully vague, so the Clan might very well be the result of hellish sorcery. It would work well with the idea that Dracula rose as a Revenant originally, and got initiated into Clan Tzimisce at Scholomance.<br /> <br /> If you don't like my work, that's fine. I'm just trying to help.</div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciate the help but still it's not exactly what I'm aiming for though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","name":"Black Blood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T16:45:33-08:00","id":1283386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Blood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula?p=1283383#post1283383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I appreciate the help but still it's not exactly what I'm aiming for though.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries. What exactly are you aiming for? What does my write up lack that you'd like to see personally?<br /> <br /> I want to make sure that when Dracula shows up in my Victorian London chronicle, I do him justice, so the opinion of someone who also wants to do Dracula justice matters to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T17:05:26-08:00","id":1283390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula?p=1283386#post1283386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No worries. What exactly are you aiming for? What does my write up lack that you'd like to see personally?<br /> <br /> I want to make sure that when Dracula shows up in my Victorian London chronicle, I do him justice, so the opinion of someone who also wants to do Dracula justice matters to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I'm aiming for basically porting the entire character from the novel into a potetial CoD game with everything else unchanged pretty much without having him as a Kindred or something like that like your writeup does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","name":"Black Blood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T17:25:26-08:00","id":1283395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Blood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula?p=1283390#post1283390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I'm aiming for basically porting the entire character from the novel into a potetial CoD game with everything else unchanged pretty much without having him as a Kindred or something like that like your writeup does.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, I do know of two types of vampires (non-kindred ones) that use magicks to empower themselves and live forever. There's the Ghuls I mentioned, and then there's the Sons of Phobos who sacrifice the hearts of the living to power their magicks and live forever. Honestly, you might want to use some of the Horror stuff from the Mortals stuff to build Dracula more to the book than the Requiem stuff seeing as the Horrors system is very build whatever you want/need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T17:45:11-08:00","id":1283398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Blood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula?p=1283390#post1283390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I'm aiming for basically porting the entire character from the novel into a potetial CoD game with everything else unchanged pretty much without having him as a Kindred or something like that like your writeup does.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're aiming for the impossible, and like someone else said: if you really want a 1 on 1 exact adaptation and don't want Dracula being Kindred, you're going to be forced to make Dracula an entirely different and unique monster, which in turn would ruin the Ordo Dracul or severely cheapen them. It would also make Dracula somewhat irrelevant for a Vampire chronicle. What would be the point of that? What do you gain in return?<br /> <br /> I think if you'd concede on him not being Kindred, and do make him Kindred, you can actually get pretty damned close to what we see in the book.<br /> <br /> To address some of your concerns and how to implement them in CofD:<br /> <br /> <b>Scholomance:</b> The book mentions this place exactly twice, in only 2 sentences total. While the book says Dracula studied there, it doesn't specifically state he became a vampire there. Suffice to say you have a lot of leeway here. You can have a Kindred Scholomance in your game to suit your needs.<br /> <br /> <b>Being able to walk in the sunlight:</b> A Kindred Dracula would be able to do this with the Mystery of the Ascendant.<br /> <br /> <b>Repelled by holy imagery:</b> This is a bane you can pick when you fail a Breaking Point. It's called Repulsion (p. 108 of VTR 2e). Kindred Dracula would have this bane.<br /> <br /> <b>No reflection and not showing up on cameras:</b> 'The Lost Visage' (p. 60 of VTR 2e) says that all vampires lack a reflection. Well, they don't, you just never see the reflection because of the Beast. Dracula's lack of reflection is merely the result of the Lost Visage, something all Kindred have. Not showing up on cameras is also a result of this. Again, something all Kindred deal with.<br /> If that isn't enough for you. Some Nosferatu actually completely lack a reflection or shadow as part of their curse, and the Hollow Mekhet have an evil spirit twin that has taken over their shadow and reflection, giving it a will of its own.<br /> <br /> <b>Red blazing inferno eyes:</b> All vampires could have this as a result of many things. Frenzy might cause this to happen. Failing to use a Discipline might cause this to happen (a Disicpline always does <i>something</i>). Or it could be the result of hunger, a bane any vampire can get, check 'Face of Hunger' on page 108 of VTR. If that isn't good enough for you, I'd once again point at the Nosferatu, who could easily have this as part of their Clan curse.<br /> <br /> <b>Aging and becoming younger after feeding:</b> This could easily tie into the Face of Hunger bane. There's also a bloodline in 1e that ages, although I forgot which bloodline it was. You could always just come up with your own unique bloodline that does this. Vampire the Requiem has plenty of room for more bloodlines.<br /> <br /> <b>Hairy and clawed hands:</b> Sounds like the Protean Discipline to me. Otherwise this could once again be the result of a Nosferatu Clan bane (I'm starting to see a trend here, maybe Dracula is part of Clan Nosferatu?).<br /> <br /> <b>Cannot cross running water:</b> This never actually happens in the book. Dracula has no problem traveling by ship or crossing bridges in his carriage. If you do insist on giving Dracula this bane. That's fine. It's already in the book, although normally reserved for Strix, it can easily be given to a Kindred as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Invitation:</b> Also an existing bane all Kindred can get. Again, see page 108 of VTR 2e.<br /> <br /> <b>Must sleep in his native soil: </b>Again, see page 108 of VTR 2e.<br /> <br /> <b>No Beast and no Humanity:</b> I think this is nonsense. There are plenty of times where Dracula in Stoker's novel succumbs to bursts of violence and anger, or bursts of strong emotions, which very much reminds me of how frenzy works in VTR 2e. There is also plenty of times the novel points out how bestial Dracula really is. But if you insist that Dracula never frenzies. Well, guess what? There are ways for Kindred to never (or hardly ever) frenzy. the Meditative Mind Merit (p. 46 of CofD) together with a high Resolve + Composure score goes a long way, and Mystery of the Wyrm also allows you to nip a frenzy in the butt by directing your Beast to retreat when you feel a frenzy boil up. Humanity is just a game system to see how close your vampire is to the Beast.<br /> <br /> <b>Sorcery:</b> If you want Dracula to be a sorcerer like in the novel. That's fine. Cruac, Theban Sorcery and Mysteries of the Dragon together cover everything Dracula can do in the novels. Coincidentally, canonically, Dracula knows all 3 of these sorceries in Vampire the Requiem.<br /> <br /> So my conclusion? Making Dracula anything else than Revenant or Kindred would cheapen the character in this setting, it wouldn't do the Requiem setting justice, it wouldn't do Dracula justice, and it wouldn't do the Ordo Dracul justice either.<br /> <br /> My advice? Keep Dracula Kindred. Apply the points I made in this post to your Dracula character (make him a Nosferatu with a unique bloodline and at least a couple of dots in Protean, Animalism and Majesty) and he will be almost identical to the novel Dracula, while also respecting the Vampire the Requiem setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 01-28-2019, 08:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T17:58:54-08:00","id":1283400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula?p=1283398#post1283398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>No Beast and no Humanity:</b> I think this is nonsense. There are plenty of times where Dracula in Stoker's novel succumbs to bursts of violence and anger, or bursts of strong emotions, which very much reminds me of how frenzy works in VTR 2e. There is also plenty of times the novel points out how bestial Dracula really is. But if you insist that Dracula never frenzies. Well, guess what? There are ways for Kindred to never (or hardly ever) frenzy. the Meditative Mind Merit (p. 46 of CofD) together with a high Resolve + Composure score goes a long way, and Mystery of the Wyrm also allows you to nip a frenzy in the butt by directing your Beast to retreat when you feel a frenzy boil up. Humanity is just a game system to see how close your vampire is to the Beast..</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Dracula's burst of violence and anger had anything to do with his vampirism but rather it's him alone since you have to remember that Novel Dracula was a complete jerk and also very clearly he was a tyrannical feudal warlord in life who was ruthless especially in battle which his 15th century habits die hard in him.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","user":"Black Blood","date":". 01-28-2019, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","name":"Black Blood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T22:28:10-08:00","id":1283441,"title":"","content":"I mean, by book in Requiem frenzy isn't always a Kuruth-esque bestial rage. It's the Beast seeing an opportunity to get what it wants, and taking the reins for a bit. Becoming captivated by the sight of blood and not being able to focus on anything else until you feed is a valid frenzy. So is going into a blind rage at a minor insult. Dracula does both in Stoker's original book.<br /> <br /> If you really want you can say &quot;he never frenzies he just does something identical to a frenzy because of who he is&quot;. But why bother?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T22:43:45-08:00","id":1283447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula?p=1283441#post1283441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, by book in Requiem frenzy isn't always a Kuruth-esque bestial rage. It's the Beast seeing an opportunity to get what it wants, and taking the reins for a bit. Becoming captivated by the sight of blood and not being able to focus on anything else until you feed is a valid frenzy. So is going into a blind rage at a minor insult. Dracula does both in Stoker's original book.<br /> <br /> If you really want you can say &quot;he never frenzies he just does something identical to a frenzy because of who he is&quot;. But why bother?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is the &quot;beast within&quot; is just a VtM/VtR invention that is never mentioned or brought up anywhere in the original novel or any 19th century Vampire literature at all.<br /> <br /> Also the reason Dracula was captivated by Blood is because he hasn't feed perhaps for a long time until maybe Harker came around.<br /> <br /> Just because there's parallels doesn't mean it's the same thing in context though although the concept of the beast may have been 'born' out of those but still taken out of context perhaps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","user":"Black Blood","date":". 01-29-2019, 01:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","name":"Black Blood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T22:54:36-08:00","id":1283450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Blood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula?p=1283447#post1283447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is the &quot;beast&quot; is just a VtM/VtR invention that is never mentioned or brought up anywhere in the original novel or any 19th century Vampire literature at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's almost like it's metaphorical nomenclature attached to existing animalistic behavioral phenomena in vampire fiction and expecting a specific term from a roleplaying game released no earlier than 1991 to be mentioned in its Victorian-era inspirations is so needlessly particular as to beggar belief.<br /> <br /> You're asking about how to make the &quot;real&quot; Dracula in the Chronicles of Darkness and you're asking it in the Vampire: the Requiem subforum. Staunch refusal to acknowledge that people are going to filter their suggestions through those facts for basically no reason makes it really hard to determine what your actual goal is here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T23:32:42-08:00","id":1283456,"title":"","content":"As I understand it the Requiem books more than hint that all of the various clans of Kindred (Ventrue, Daeva, Gangrel etc...) were originally different creatures with their own, unique, lost in the mists of time origins and it was only long term interaction between them that created the similar modern Kindred.<br /> Given that there is no reason, even in canon, why there can't be a totally unrelated creature with a unique origin of its own stalking the land.<br /> So make your Dracula exactly how you envision him from the novel, give him a snowflake origin with super special strengths and weaknesses exactly how you envision and don't worry about how he relates to the Kindred. <br /> He only has to mesh with them in two ways:<br /> 1-Whatever you make him he has to work within the mechanics of the game, when he rolls dice or an opponent rolls dice against him you have to know what the end result will be.<br /> 2-If he is still the founder of the Order Dracul then you will need to decide, at least in vague terms, what that actually means. I will remind you that the Order is exactly that, its not a clan or even bloodline but a group that a Kindred of any background can potentially join. There is no reason why a Vampire of a different sort couldn't have played a part in teaching its Kindred members, either intentionally or through being studied, how to nearly duplicate its own unique abilities. That could even go a long way towards explaining why the Order hasn't perfected its Coils yet.<br /> <br /> Make him whatever you want, just decide what that means and how he will interact with the Kindred that probably make up most of the game world. At least enough to tell your story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T07:29:58-08:00","id":1283504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1282771-the-actual-origin-of-dracula?p=1283450#post1283450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's almost like it's metaphorical nomenclature attached to existing animalistic behavioral phenomena in vampire fiction and expecting a specific term from a roleplaying game released no earlier than 1991 to be mentioned in its Victorian-era inspirations is so needlessly particular as to beggar belief.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then again not all Vampire literature in the 19th century had animalistic behavior phenomena existing particularly Polidari's &quot;Vampyr&quot; which Ruthven for example never displayed such behavior but rather he was more of a serial killer biting down and tearing the flesh of the women that fall in love with him using the strength of his jaw and he has no fangs either. The earliest example of Fangs were from &quot;Varney the Vampire&quot; which I think was the earliest description of having insable blood hunger only under the light of the full moon and the earliest example of Vampire fiction to regard vampirism as a 'curse' more because it has to do with Varney paying for his crimes he did in life which is why the Full Moon like Ruthven keeps reviving him.<br /> <br /> Then again just because the animalistic behaviors existed in said vampire stories doesn't mean it's the beast from a VtM/VtR context though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","user":"Black Blood","date":". 01-29-2019, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","name":"Black Blood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T08:12:46-08:00","id":1283508,"title":"","content":"Ayup. Also, refer to &quot;Count F****** Dracula&quot; on DriveThruRPG (down as of this typing). I rather like that little piece as Dracula reinventing himself for the modern era. <br /> <br /> But again to the point: we don't know if Dracula is better as a real person or a symbol the Brides used to kickstart the Ordo, which certainly needed enough adopters to come together and share their insights into vampirism and how to rise above it, if it was to function as an academic institution with practical side-effects.<br /> <br /> It could <i>all</i> be a lie.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T10:14:35-08:00","id":1283532,"title":"","content":"@Black Blood<br /> <br /> I kind of want to echo 2ptTakrill. How were you thinking of having Dracula play out? I know you haven't got a game and are just brainstorming, but what direction are you thinking of going with the idea?<br /> <br /> Like, we can just take it for granted that Dracula isn't Kindred and that Stoker's novel is an accurate historical document in your world. But without more of a sense of what you want to focus on, we're left with a &quot;so what?&quot; response.<br /> <br /> Do you want to brainstorm on what events occurred post-novel or are you looking to create a new minor-template? Or are you trying to think of the consequences on the Ordo? Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T17:35:23-08:00","id":1283603,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7348\" data-vbnamecard=\"7348\">Black Blood</a><br /> <br /> I would also like to add that 'the Beast' in Vampire the Requiem is not necessarily a literal separate entity that hides inside the Kindred. The Kindred like to talk about 'the Beast' as something other than themselves because they don't like to face the facts that <i>they</i> are the monsters, and that <i>they</i> are responsible for all the people <i>they</i> killed in a bloodthirsty rage. Some Clans are more honest about it than others, the Gangrel seem to be most aware of the fact that they are the Beast and the Beast is them.<br /> <br /> 'The Beast' is also an umbrella term in the VtR meta for us roleplayers and storytellers to group a certain set of vampire behaviors under one label so we have something to refer to when dealing with vampiric bloodthirst, vampiric rage and animalistic behavior.<br /> <br /> The same goes for 'Humanity' by the way. It's a label vampires (but also us the players and storytellers) use to categorize humane behavior, in contrast to the distinctly inhumane behavior that falls under the 'Beast' label.<br /> <br /> I think if you want to look at what the Beast and Humanity <i>really</i> represent, you should read Sigmund Freud's <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Id,_ego_and_super-ego\" target=\"_blank\">structural model of the human psyche</a> where he describes the Id, Ego and Super-Ego. The Beast is nothing more than a person's Id turned up to eleven, and Humanity is nothing more than a person's Super-Ego.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}